.TH SINDOOK-REWRAP 1 "2026-08-31" "sindook 0.11.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sindook-rewrap \- rotate recipients, passphrases, or the file key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sindook rewrap
[\fB\-i\fP \fIIDENTITY\fP | \fB\-p\fP | \fB\-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP]
[\fB\-identity-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP]
[\fB\-keep\fP] [\fB\-drop-slot\fP \fIN\fP]...
[\fB\-drop-i\fP \fIIDENTITY\fP]... [\fB\-drop-p\fP]
[\fB\-drop-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP]... [\fB\-drop-pass-slots\fP]
[\fB\-r\fP \fIRECIPIENT\fP]...
[\fB\-R\fP \fIFILE\fP]... [\fB\-new-passphrase\fP |
\fB\-new-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP] [\fB\-glob\fP \fIPATTERN\fP]...
[\fB\-deep\fP] [\fB\-o\fP \fIOUT\fP] [\fB\-f\fP] \fIFILE\fP...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replaces the key slots of sealed files. With no unlocking credential
flag, the identity selected by
.BR sindook-init (1)
is used when one exists. By default fast mode preserves
the payload ciphertext without decrypting or re-encrypting it, then
copies that ciphertext to a replacement file with a fresh header.
Fast mode does not revoke someone who kept a copy of the old file.
\fB\-deep\fP creates a replacement with a fresh file key, so removed
recipients cannot open that replacement using the old file key.
Files are staged beside their original path and replaced only after a
successful write unless \fB\-o\fP is given. Rotating a whole directory
of files in one run is the intended use. Fast rewrap also upgrades v1
files to the current format in place.
.PP
By default the replacement slot set is exactly the
\fB\-r\fP/\fB\-R\fP/\fB\-new\-*\fP arguments. With \fB\-keep\fP the
existing slots are preserved and those arguments append to them; the
\fB\-drop\-\fP* flags remove matching slots from the kept set and imply
\fB\-keep\fP. Slot numbers are the ones
.BR sindook-inspect (1)
prints. Every drop selector must match at least one slot, and an edit
may not leave a file with no slots. \fB\-deep\fP cannot be combined
with \fB\-keep\fP or \fB\-drop\-\fP*: a fresh file key and nonce
invalidate every kept slot.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fP \fIIDENTITY\fP
identity that opens the files today; use \fB@default\fP for the
identity selected by
.BR sindook-init (1) ;
with no credential flag at all, that default identity is used when
one exists
.TP
\fB\-p\fP
open with the current passphrase (prompted)
.TP
\fB\-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP
read the current passphrase from \fIFILE\fP
.TP
\fB\-identity-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP
read a protected identity's passphrase from \fIFILE\fP; applies to
\fB\-i\fP and \fB\-drop-i\fP files alike
.TP
\fB\-keep\fP
preserve existing key slots; drops and additions apply on top of them.
Kept slots are copied verbatim, so passphrases stay in place without
being re-entered
.TP
\fB\-drop-slot\fP \fIN\fP
drop slot \fIN\fP as listed by
.BR sindook-inspect (1) ,
repeatable; implies \fB\-keep\fP
.TP
\fB\-drop-i\fP \fIIDENTITY\fP
drop every slot that opens under \fIIDENTITY\fP, repeatable; implies
\fB\-keep\fP. The file is loaded like \fB\-i\fP, including protected
identities
.TP
\fB\-drop-p\fP
drop every slot that opens under a prompted passphrase; implies
\fB\-keep\fP
.TP
\fB\-drop-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP
drop every slot that opens under the passphrase in \fIFILE\fP,
repeatable; implies \fB\-keep\fP
.TP
\fB\-drop-pass-slots\fP
drop every passphrase slot; implies \fB\-keep\fP
.TP
\fB\-r\fP \fIRECIPIENT\fP
new recipient, repeatable
.TP
\fB\-R\fP \fIFILE\fP
file of new recipients, one key per line, repeatable
.TP
\fB\-new-passphrase\fP
add a new passphrase slot (prompted)
.TP
\fB\-new-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP
read the new passphrase from \fIFILE\fP
.TP
\fB\-glob\fP \fIPATTERN\fP
add files matched by a portable filesystem pattern, repeatable
.TP
\fB\-deep\fP
re-encrypt the payload under a fresh file key
.TP
\fB\-o\fP \fIOUT\fP
output path, \fB\-\fP for stdout (single \fIFILE\fP only)
.TP
\fB\-f\fP
overwrite existing output
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sindook rewrap -i my.key -r alice.pub -r bob.pub archive.tar.sindook
sindook rewrap -i my.key -keep -r carol.pub shared.sindook
sindook rewrap -i my.key -drop-slot 2 shared.sindook
sindook rewrap -i my.key -drop-i old.key -r new.pub *.sindook
sindook rewrap -i my.key -drop-pass-slots recipients-only.sindook
sindook rewrap -i my.key -r alice.pub -deep archive.tar.sindook
sindook rewrap -i old.key -R team.keys backups/*.sindook
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sindook (1),
.BR sindook-seal (1),
.BR sindook-open (1),
.BR sindook-inspect (1)
